  "notes": "USAGE:\n{隣接|りんせつ} is a formal, written-style word meaning physically adjacent or sharing a border. It is commonly used in real estate, geography, and urban planning.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- AはBに{隣接|りんせつ}している (A is adjacent to B)\n- Bに{隣接|りんせつ}したA (A which is adjacent to B)\n- {隣接|りんせつ}するA (adjoining A)\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {隣接|りんせつ}する{地域|ちいき} (adjacent area)\n- {隣接|りんせつ}する{国|くに} (neighboring country)\n- ～に{隣接|りんせつ}している (to be adjacent to ~)\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {隣接|りんせつ}: adjacent, adjoining (formal; sharing a border)\n- {隣|となり}: next door, neighboring (everyday, casual)\n- {近隣|きんりん}: neighborhood, vicinity (nearby area in general)",
